<title>FINLAND: FINNISH EXPORT CREDIT SETS $10 MLN ARGENTINA LOAN.</title>
<headline>FINNISH EXPORT CREDIT SETS $10 MLN ARGENTINA LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Export Credit Ltd said on Monday it had sealed a five-year framework agreement with Banco de Galicia y Buenos Aires on a $10 million framework loan to promote Finnish exports to Argentina.</p>
<p>&quot;The amount of the framework loan granted by Finnish Export Credit Ltd is $10 million or about 50 million markka,&quot; Finnish Export Credit Ltd said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The framework loan will be used to finance deliveries of Finnish capital goods and related services,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The loan was agreed in connection with a visit to Argentina by Finnish president Martti Ahtisaari, Finnish Export Credit Ltd said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235, news@reuters.fi</p>
